// The only place the example's Idura Verify configuration is written on iOS, so
// Info.plist and Runner.entitlements cannot end up disagreeing about the domain.
// The Android side reaches the same guarantee with two Gradle
// manifestPlaceholders.
//
// Included from Debug.xcconfig and Release.xcconfig rather than set on the
// target, so the values live in git rather than buried in project.pbxproj, and
// so CODE_SIGN_ENTITLEMENTS reaches Runner only — the RunnerTests
// configurations have no base configuration to pick it up from.
//
// Same tenant the native Android and iOS examples use.
IDURA_DOMAIN = samples-flutter.test.idura.broker
IDURA_CLIENT_ID = urn:criipto:samples:idura:verify-flutter

// Without this the login callback never comes back: iOS only hands an
// ASWebAuthenticationSession result to an app whose entitlement claims the
// domain. Always absent on the Simulator, which is why no flow runs there.
CODE_SIGN_ENTITLEMENTS = Runner/Runner.entitlements
